# Change the signed-in user. Start the API with Aspire first, then send "Create an account" once.
@host = http://localhost:5279

### Create an account → 201. The requests below use its access token.
# @name createAccount
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user-{{$guid}}@example.com",
  "password": "password",
  "timeZone": "Europe/Zagreb"
}

### Set up the name and units → 200 with the user.
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Filip",
  "units": "imperial"
}

### Change only the time zone → 200. The name and units stay the same.
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "timeZone": "Europe/London"
}

### Invalid fields → 400 validation, with errors for name and timeZone.
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": " ",
  "timeZone": "Mars/Olympus"
}

### Units that don't exist → 400 bad_request. The body can't be read, so there are no field errors.
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "units": "stones"
}

### Not signed in → 401 unauthorized.
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Filip"
}
